# What NOT to upload to Vercel.
#
# These stay in the repository -- they are part of the project and worth showing
# on GitHub -- but none of them run in production, and together they are ~48MB
# uploaded on every deploy.
#
# NOTE ON THE LEADING SLASHES. This file uses .gitignore pattern syntax, where a
# pattern without a leading slash matches a directory of that name AT ANY DEPTH.
# Writing `AI/` here excluded the Python folder AND src/components/AI,
# src/lib/ai and src/app/api/ai, which failed the build with
# "Module not found: Can't resolve '@/components/AI/PoseEngine'".
# Anchor anything meant to match only the repository root.

# The Python reference implementation. The pose analysis it defines was ported
# to JavaScript (src/lib/ai/) and runs in the browser, so Vercel never executes
# any of this. See AI/README.md.
/AI/

# Spec documents.
/document/

# Personal working notes, already gitignored but listed for completeness.
/BACKEND_GUIDE.md
/BACKEND_PROGRESS.md
/mongo.guide.md

# Local env backup. .env* files are never uploaded by Vercel anyway --
# environment variables are configured in the project settings instead.
/.env.local.bak

# Python bytecode. Unanchored on purpose: these should go wherever they appear.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
